  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.TitleAdd">Add remote device</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Name">Name (your choice)</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.AddressHint">Host and port, for example 192.168.1.42:22000. Without a port, 22000 is assumed. Leave it empty to ask the discovery server where the device is on every connect.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.DeviceId">Remote device ID</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.IdHint">In the remote device’s Syncthing UI under “This Device → Identification”.</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.AutoConnect">Connect automatically at startup</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Discovery">Look up the address on the discovery server</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.Relay">Connect through a relay when there is no direct route</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="S.Peer.RelayHint">Both are for a remote device with no port open to the outside. A relay runs on someone else’s bandwidth and is slower than any direct route — it is used only when no direct one can be made.</s:String>
